# Grafana Tempo 1.5.1 in the Tempo data-source plugin bundled with grafana/grafana:13.2.6, fixed in
# Tempo 2.10.3; 13.2.6 and 13.3.1 (2026-11-10) are the newest tags and still ship it. The plugin only
# queries the trace store of the stack, and the dashboard tool listens only on 127.0.0.1 until TLS
# exists (R14). Upstream must rebuild the plugin.
CVE-2026-21728 exp:2027-01-11
CVE-2026-28377 exp:2027-01-11

# golang.org/x/net/html (denial of service when parsing crafted HTML, fixed in x/net 0.62.0) in the
# caddy binary of caddy:2.11-alpine (x/net 0.60, build of 2026-11-13), the MongoDB database tools of
# mongo:8.0, grafana:13.2.6 and its plugins, prometheus v3.15.1 (v3.16.0 still ships 0.61), and
# tempo 2.10.10. None of them parses HTML from outside: the local proxy forwards requests, the
# stack never runs the database tools, and the observability services listen only on 127.0.0.1 or
# the internal network. Upstream must rebuild the images.
CVE-2026-78661 exp:2027-01-11

# Added 2026-11-24 (#171): libxml2 2.13.9-r2 (information disclosure, SSRF, or denial of service)
# in postgres:18-alpine of 2026-11-21; the fixed Alpine package 2.13.9-r3 came out after the image
# was built. libxml2 is only reached through the XML functions of PostgreSQL, which no unit of the
# stack calls, and the database listens only on 127.0.0.1. Upstream must rebuild the image.
CVE-2026-86144 exp:2027-01-11
